prey is proving to be a hit for critics  and fans alike but how do indigenous  film reviewers feel about this comanche  woman vs space monster flick since its  premiere on august 5th hulu's prey has  become a welcome example of big budget  filmmaking with authentic native  american representation in addition to  responding favorably to the film's story  critics have praised the film's focus on  indigenous culture with some even  calling it one of the most realistic and  honest period pieces in cinematic  history prey producer jane myers  reportedly poured her heart and soul  into the predator prequel using her  knowledge and experience as a member of  the comanche nation to help construct  scenes and props evidently the cast was  every bit as dedicated in fact pray made  hollywood history before it even hit  hulu by being a big budget franchise  film with a majority indigenous cast  additionally many cast members including  lead star amber mid thunder have spent a  lot of time talking about the sci-fi  thriller's dedication to historical  accuracy according to mid thunder  delivering an accurate representation of  indigenous peoples was of the utmost  importance to her and it seems like the  rest of the crew was similarly invested  so how does the indigenous community  feel about the film now that it's out in  her review of prey film critic and a  tribe called geek founder johnny j  referred to prey as a groundbreaking  achievement for the entire comanche  nation jay who is from the otto missouri  and choctaw tribes of oklahoma wrote it  is so much more than just another  predator movie it is a rare tribute to  the indigenity strength and sheer  stubbornness that has allowed native  people to survive the forces that  threaten our survival  i've been practicing  it's time i'm ready jay pointed out in  her review that the film was originally  intended to be fully shot in comanche  rather than english but director dan  trachtenberg decided to go with two  different versions the main version in  english and a fully dubbed comanche cut  according to jay it's the first film to  be released in both comanche and english  she wrote in her review i highly  recommend only watching the comanche  version of prey it is an incredible  opportunity to watch a movie entirely in  comanche but there's also a lot of humor  and essential nuances that get lost in  the english version expand your horizons  and watch the comanche version the movie  star amber mid thunder is also  apparently a massive fan of the comanche  dubbing she told the digital fix working  with real comanche language speakers and  people who devote their lives to the  preservation of their own language was  the opportunity of a lifetime it's  special in so many ways vincent  schilling founder and editor of native  viewpoint similarly described prey as a  film that manages to represent  indigenous people masterfully while also  holding up as an incredible action film  indeed many critics have said that the  film deserves to be ranked among the  best of the predator movies schilling  wrote i was admittedly nervous in one  sense because as a native american  journalist i have seen my share of  predatory behavior against native  communities in history but due to the  diligence of dan trachtenberg and jane  myers as well as others the film doesn't  come across as though the native  warriors are just cannon fodder  schilling also noted that it was clear  that the producers of the film paid  supreme diligence to the cultural  accuracy of the film he continued for  once as a native man i could actually  relax and enjoy a film without waiting  for the culturally inappropriate bomb to  drop  why do you want to hunt  because you all think that i can't  when it came to the interactions with  settlers and non-native peoples  chilling's only complaint for pretty  much the entire movie was that they  seemed like overly clumsy fools but as  you wrote perhaps that was the point if  these writers are any indication it  appears that indigenous critics are huge  fans of prey schilling wrote in his  review the biggest feeling i have  overall is that the film was simply  fantastic shout out to all the cast and  crew for doing an exceptional job you  made this mohawk film reviewer proud  [Music]
 

